Looking at this problem, I need to solve the recurrence, use the condition $2010 \mid a_{2009}$ to constrain the sequence, then find the smallest $n \geq 2$ with $2010 \mid a_n$.

## Setting Up the Recurrence

The recurrence $n(a_{n+1} - a_n + 3) = a_{n+1} + a_n + 3$ rearranges to:
$$(n-1)a_{n+1} = (n+1)a_n - 3(n-1)$$

At $n = 1$: this gives $0 = 2a_1$, forcing $a_1 = 0$ (even), contradicting "$a_1$ is odd." So the recurrence governs $n \geq 2$, and $a_1$ is a free odd parameter independent of the rest of the sequence.

## Solving the Recurrence (for $n \geq 2$)

Substitute $a_n = (n-1)b_n$:
$$n\,b_{n+1} = (n+1)b_n - 3$$

Set $b_n = 3 + c_n$. Then $n\,c_{n+1} = (n+1)c_n$, so $\frac{c_{n+1}}{n+1} = \frac{c_n}{n}$, giving $c_n = nk$ for a constant $k$.

Thus $b_n = 3 + nk$ and:
$$a_n = (n-1)(3 + nk) = \frac{(n-1)(6 + nm)}{2}, \quad n \geq 2$$
where $m = 2k$ is an integer (since $a_2 = 3 + m$ is an integer). One verifies $(n-1)(6+nm)$ is always even, so all $a_n$ are integers.

## Applying $2010 \mid a_{2009}$

